From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: clock: mediatek: add the MT6897 display and codec clock gates

Add the clock gate blocks of the MediaTek MT6897 display, MDP and video
codec hardware: dispsys0, dispsys1, ovlsys0, ovlsys1, mminfra, mdpsys0,
mdpsys1, vdecsys, vdecsys-soc, vencsys and vencsys-c1, with their clock
identifiers. The identifiers follow the tables of the MediaTek vendor
driver (OnePlus Pad GPL release).

The display blocks switch part of their gates through the hardware voter
and mminfra all of them, like part of pericfg_ao.

The blocks only answer while their power domain is on, but they carry no
power-domains property. The VEN and MDP power domains need gates of the
blocks they power to come up, so a power domain and its clock controller
would wait for each other. For the other blocks, runtime PM would power
the domain up and down at probe and mminfra with it, which turns off the
display the bootloader left running. A consumer powers the domain with
its own power-domains property before it enables a gate.

---
 .../bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml     |  42 ++-
 include/dt-bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.h | 278 ++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 318 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml
index fd3ad4e59..2d0bc6781 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml
@@ -21,6 +21,14 @@ description: |
   two UFS blocks also provide the reset lines of the UFS M-PHY, UniPro,
   inline crypto engine and host controller.
 
+  The display, MDP and video codec blocks only answer while their power domain
+  is on, and they have no power-domains property. The VEN and MDP power domains
+  need gates of these blocks to come up, so the two would wait for each other.
+  For the other blocks, runtime PM would power the domain up and down at probe
+  and mminfra with it, which turns off the display the bootloader left running.
+  A consumer powers the domain up with its own power-domains property before it
+  enables a gate.
+
   The identifiers of the clocks are in
   include/dt-bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.h and those of the resets
   in include/dt-bindings/reset/mediatek,mt6897-resets.h.
@@ -29,14 +37,25 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     items:
       - enum:
+          - mediatek,mt6897-dispsys0
+          - mediatek,mt6897-dispsys1
           - mediatek,mt6897-imp-iic-wrap-c
           - mediatek,mt6897-imp-iic-wrap-en
           - mediatek,mt6897-imp-iic-wrap-es
           - mediatek,mt6897-imp-iic-wrap-n
           - mediatek,mt6897-imp-iic-wrap-s
+          - mediatek,mt6897-mdpsys0
+          - mediatek,mt6897-mdpsys1
+          - mediatek,mt6897-mminfra
+          - mediatek,mt6897-ovlsys0
+          - mediatek,mt6897-ovlsys1
           - mediatek,mt6897-pericfg-ao
           - mediatek,mt6897-ufscfg-ao
           - mediatek,mt6897-ufscfg-pdn
+          - mediatek,mt6897-vdecsys
+          - mediatek,mt6897-vdecsys-soc
+          - mediatek,mt6897-vencsys
+          - mediatek,mt6897-vencsys-c1
       - const: syscon
 
   reg:
@@ -54,7 +73,7 @@ properties:
       Phandle to the hardware voter (HWV) register block. The HWV is a
       SoC-internal MCU that collects clock votes from the application
       processor and the remote processors. On MT6897 it opens and closes
-      some of the pericfg_ao gates.
+      some of the pericfg_ao, display and mminfra gates.
 
 required:
   - compatible
@@ -66,7 +85,13 @@ allOf:
       properties:
         compatible:
           contains:
-            const: mediatek,mt6897-pericfg-ao
+            enum:
+              - mediatek,mt6897-dispsys0
+              - mediatek,mt6897-dispsys1
+              - mediatek,mt6897-mminfra
+              - mediatek,mt6897-ovlsys0
+              - mediatek,mt6897-ovlsys1
+              - mediatek,mt6897-pericfg-ao
     then:
       required:
         - mediatek,hardware-voter
@@ -110,3 +135,16 @@ examples:
         reg = <0x11f02000 0x1000>;
         #clock-cells = <1>;
     };
+  - |
+    clock-controller@14000000 {
+        compatible = "mediatek,mt6897-dispsys0", "syscon";
+        reg = <0x14000000 0x1000>;
+        mediatek,hardware-voter = <&hwv>;
+        #clock-cells = <1>;
+    };
+  - |
+    clock-controller@17000000 {
+        compatible = "mediatek,mt6897-vencsys", "syscon";
+        reg = <0x17000000 0x1000>;
+        #clock-cells = <1>;
+    };
